[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3293090531","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110534#issuecomment-3293090531","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110534","id":3293090531,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ESJLj","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-15T16:54:17Z","updated_at":"2025-09-15T16:54:17Z","body":"Because you are using the same 3d render scenario for everything.\n\nEvery Viewport creates a dedicated 2D canvas to rendering its 2d stuff, but for 3D, the 3d render scenario is shared across all Viewports, always using the root Viewport scenario by default.\n\nYou need to either create a dedicated scenario using the RenderingServer API or add a dedicated own World3D resource to the SubViewport node that you are using.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3293090531/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3293339351","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110534#issuecomment-3293339351","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110534","id":3293339351,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ETF7X","user":{"login":"96Bysc","id":191048877,"node_id":"U_kgDOC2MsrQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191048877?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc","html_url":"https://github.com/96Bysc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/96Bysc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-15T18:02:34Z","updated_at":"2025-09-15T18:02:34Z","body":"> Because you are using the same 3d render scenario for everything.\n> \n> Every Viewport creates a dedicated 2D canvas to rendering its 2d stuff, but for 3D, the 3d render scenario is shared across all Viewports, always using the root Viewport scenario by default.\n> \n> You need to either create a dedicated scenario using the RenderingServer API or add a dedicated own World3D resource to the SubViewport node that you are using.\n\nI don't think it's an intended feature because the SubViewport doesn't work as it says that it should in the documentation. And the bug is not reproducible in Godot 4.3","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/i